{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An editor agent can read the plaintext credentials during deployment, with a longer exposure window on certain failure or relaunch paths."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A timed-out launchctl inspection can falsely fail a live deployment and remove the marker that prevents a subsequent relaunch from deploying again."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"diag","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A redaction filter setup failure can silently discard deployment logs, but the reproduced deployment still completes and the daemon normally writes valid credentials immediately beforehand."}]}